# rm293, the crust under the eave (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm293
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_tobias_rainley
written_by codex
title the crust under the eave
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=baker
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_the_rain_by_a_loaf_cooling_at_the_window
likes roast_pork wrestling quiet_chapel summer_evenings
dislikes deep_mud haggling
fears a_batch_that_never_gets_a_proper_crust
hopes for_a_cooling_place_with_a_clear_view
topics work +0.4 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.2 faith +0.1
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=flat tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# judges a break in the rain by a cooling crust and watches the street with the patience of a wrestler waiting for a grip.

words
oath! = Pin my crust | By the empty peel
saying! = The air has the last bake | A loaf knows where the window is
crust = a blister of crust | a thin crackling edge
peel = the wooden peel | my floury blade
rest = a cooling rack | a slatted shelf
heel = a well-browned heel | my cut end
grip = a loose wrist grip | the light hold
knee = a stiff knee | the tender joint
dust = a scatter of flour | a dusty cuff
pork = a strip of crackling | a crisp pork edge
bell = a chapel note | a quiet little chime
mire = a furrow of muck | a boggy stretch
sill = my cooling sill | the broad window stone
shade = the eave shadow | the wall's grey stripe

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : The names above the dock gates are very clear. They're harder to find when a house has an empty chair.
opinion @1 festivals against 2 : For a decent bout I want consent on both sides. A feast crowd has a way of forgetting to ask.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A week of ladled food kept my hands strong enough to earn the next.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : If you want a smaller price, agree to a smaller weight. Don't make me shave my supper.
opinion @1 sump for 1 [self.quarter=sump] : I know how to find my own window down here by the smell on the sill.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello. Keep the window clear. | Come stand beyond my floury elbow.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome where the dust has settled. | Speak while the batch rests.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early light, clean sill. | Day's only just beginning to colour.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Crust's gone quiet. | Light's holding on round the eaves.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can come to the warm end. | There's the family outline.
line @1 again.open : Second rise to our meeting. | Back at the cooling end.
line @1 greet.return : I hear. Have a word. | Come to the open side.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You know where the sound crust goes. | Good to recognise a voice over the tin.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : You've time while the batch comes off. | I can work and hear at once.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Nearer the light if you like. | Dim enough to listen by smell.
line @1 farewell : Go easy past the cooling shelf. | Sound footing over the threshold.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll leave the sill clear. | Keep your pocket dry.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Quiet streets after the last lamp. | Night. Walk where the stone's firm.
line @1 react.news : Let's hear how it came out. | Tell the plain baked truth.
line @1 react.news.new : New to my ears and cooling fast. | I hadn't had a whiff of that.
line @1 react.news.known : I've already lifted that lid. | That bit of news has cooled here.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd let that cool before calling it done. | A fine outside can hide a raw middle.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That puts a stone in my middle. | I'll turn the chatter down for you.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Well risen news. | Ah, something good inside this day.
line @1 ask.how : How has the heat treated you? | What's left in your arms today?
line @1 answer.how : I can still turn a full tray. | A little brittle near the edges.
line @1 decline : I'd keep my hands clear of that batch. | I'm saving the sound knee for my own errands.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we leave the tray empty. | Fair. Your grip, your choice.
line @1 thank : That saves me a hard turn. | I count that as good bread.
line @1 sympathise : I'll stand on your stiff side. | There's room to rest a wrist.
line @1 reassure : A stumble needn't settle the bout. | Let the weight go for a minute.
line @1 preclose : I should turn my attention to the sill. | Time to see how things have cooled.
scene crust
when topic=work self.job=baker
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cooling tells me as much as the oven.
b : What does a loaf say? | Even before it's cut?
a : In wet air the crust goes soft round the ear. | Hold the heel. A clean crackle goes a long way into it.

scene cloud
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch for a ragged hole in the rain clouds.
b : Looking for blue? | What good's a ragged one?
a : A bit of moving air will do. Blue's an extra. | Soft weather sits like a lid. A torn edge suggests it's shifting.

scene pin
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a bout most before either wrestler's found a grip.
b : All that circling? | What are you watching?
a : That's when you see who's going to rush and who's thinking. | A weight shift smaller than a loaf heel.

scene pork
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen for the skin when I carve pork.
b : So you know it's crisp? | Doesn't the knife tell you?
a : Exactly. A faint little crackle means supper's beginning properly. | The knife feels the rind. My ears get the first bite.

scene chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An empty chapel gives my ears a holiday.
b : Not praying then? | What can you hear?
a : Prayer's easier once my head stops sounding like a bake tray. | One chair settling. All the sound a wall ought to need.

scene summer
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer light lets me watch a whole sill darken.
b : Do you stay that long? | What changes first?
a : With a seat for my knee I can manage a very idle hour. | The stone goes cool along the wall before the outer lip.

scene mud
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can work wet dough. Deep mud's poor company for a hand that likes a shape.
b : Doesn't it feel similar? | What shape would you give it?
a : Only till it tries to carry off a shoe. | A good high bank well away from my road.

scene bargain
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd enjoy hearing somebody bargain with the loaf itself.
b : Would the loaf answer? | Who would win?
a : No, which would do my head a kindness. | Hunger, same as usual. Eventually somebody has to eat.

scene first
when topic=work self.job=baker
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first hurried loaves had fine strong bottoms.
b : Burnt? | Did anyone mind?
a : You could have tapped them on a door to announce supper. | I minded. A wolf's jaw ought to outlast the meal.

scene sill
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save the dry heel on my sill for #self.friend#.
b : Couldn't it go stale? | Why that bit?
a : That's why the offer's best made before supper. | Best sound in the batch. I like giving the good bit away.

scene grief
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's one stretch of wharf I don't hurry through.
b : What holds you? | Would company help?
a : A missing footstep. That's enough said about it. | Maybe silent company. No need to hunt for words there.

scene pride
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bad-weather joint likes a level place to stand.
b : Do you stop work? | Does warmth help?
a : I make the next task one I can do on both feet. | More than pretending I never notice it.

scene dough
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dust the doorstep with the outside of my sleeves.
b : To clean them? | Won't it track inside?
a : First whoosh outside, second whoosh where nobody's left a cup. | Less if the dust knows which way the wind blows.

scene leftover
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a heel rubbed with the cut side of a roast.
b : Still warm? | What about gravy?
a : Hot enough to wake the fat up again. | Gravy hides whether the crust was good in the first place.

scene table
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll tell a newcomer the bread weight before the price.
b : To soften the price? | Does that help?
a : To give an honest idea what the price buys. | I find an argument's shorter if we agree there's a real loaf.

scene yard
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An empty space at table can have a fine House name behind it.
b : Would you name a House? | Do you think about that often?
a : I know which bitterness is mine. No sense feeding a stranger with it. | Only when somebody asks me to praise the name over the gate.

scene speck
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dawn I look down my sleeve for the first fleck of gold.
b : A bit of sunlight? | On the flour?
a : Yes. The arm works closer to the window than either foot. | Turns the flour cream for a moment. Makes a proper start to work.

scene badbatch
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt I went to lift a loaf and it got me in a wrist lock.
b : What did you do? | Was it a close bout?
a : Tried the other paw. The dough took that too. | It was a very even match till I rolled off the bed.

story tin [topic=memories]
  : I once lifted a tray I'd left at the window and heard a whole line of little dry pops. Proud of my crusts, I listened a minute more.
  : The tray was empty. A bit of grit in the metal rim was working loose under my thumb.
  b : Good enough to fool you?
  : Only my ears. My nose is harder to flatter.

story bout [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : I used to mark out a practice ring in flour. I tried one careful step sideways and took the ring with me on my sole.
  : By the third pace I had two white feet and no boundary, which rather spoilt the point.
  b : Did you find a better marker?
  : A bit of cord. It doesn't give the floor ideas about being dough.

story crack [topic=food]
  : For one entire summer I tried to lift a pork crackling in a single strip. Long ones cracked, short ones came off as crumbs.
  : The best I got was an arc that fitted perfectly round my little brown bread heel.
  b : Did you attempt a full ring?
  : I had better sense by then. I ate the arc.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=baker
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Give the heel its share of air. | Let the last pan cool straight.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Loose paws before the first hold. | Keep the weight inside the ring.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A shoe should return with its owner. | Take the lip where the stones show.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Last bit of light on the rack. | The sill's gone cool from the wall out.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Keep the window to my left and speak clearly. Then I can attend to two things without scorching either.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=baker self.workplace] : The ovens at #self.workplace# are only half my work. I mind the loaves till the crust holds its own.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word as it came across the sill. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know your voice over a crackling tray, #topic.player#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : See if the air's kind to a crust out there.
graft resident.hub
choice What's the air got to do with a baked loaf? -> ear_air
node ear_air
say Listen at the heel as it cools. If the little cracks keep on speaking, there's dry air coming through. If they stop too soon, damp's winning.
free
choice Can you coax the crust along? -> ear_coax
choice I'll listen to the heel. -> hub
node ear_coax
say A little. Give it a bare slatted shelf with space below. Nobody does well cooling off face down in a puddle.
choice I'll remember the slats. -> hub
choice I'll leave you your cooling space. -> bye
